{"id":814,"date":"2025-08-21T11:33:20","date_gmt":"2025-08-21T11:33:20","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/bombayfoodstuff.com\/bombayfoodstuff\/?post_type=product&#038;p=814"},"modified":"2025-08-26T08:01:36","modified_gmt":"2025-08-26T08:01:36","slug":"mace","status":"publish","type":"product","link":"https:\/\/bombayfoodstuff.com\/product\/mace\/","title":{"rendered":"Mace (Javitri)"},"content":{"rendered":"<h2><b>Mace (Javitri)<\/b><\/h2>\n<p><b>Hindi Name:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Javitri<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br \/>\n<\/span><b>Botanical Name:<\/b> <i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Myristica fragrans<\/span><\/i><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br \/>\n<\/span><\/i><b>Family Name:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Myristicaceae<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br \/>\n<\/span><b>Commercial Part:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Aril (the bright red lacy covering of nutmeg seed)<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>Product Description<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mace, known as <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Javitri<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in Hindi, is the delicate, bright red aril that surrounds the nutmeg seed. Once separated and dried, it forms lacy blades with a warm, aromatic, and slightly sweet-spicy flavor. Valued for its unique fragrance and subtle pungency, mace has been cherished for centuries in culinary, medicinal, and flavoring applications.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Unlike nutmeg, mace offers a lighter, more refined taste, making it ideal for flavoring delicate dishes. Whole mace blades retain aroma longer, while ground mace provides ease of use in food processing.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>Culinary Uses<\/b><\/h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Enhances milk-based dishes such as <\/span><b>custards, puddings, cream sauces, and desserts<\/b>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Used in <\/span><b>cakes, pastries, donuts, and confectionery<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for a warm sweet note<\/span>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Popular in <\/span><b>clear soups, casseroles, chicken pies, and sauces<\/b>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A key ingredient in <\/span><b>spice blends, pickles, and marinades<\/b>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Adds depth to <\/span><b>curries, biryanis, and Mughlai gravies<\/b>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h3><b>Nutritional &amp; Medicinal Value<\/b><\/h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rich in essential oils that aid digestion and improve appetite<\/span>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Contains <\/span><b>vitamins A, C, and B-complex<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> along with essential minerals like <\/span><b>iron, copper, and manganese<\/b>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Traditionally used in Ayurveda and Unani medicine for its <\/span><b>anti-inflammatory and digestive properties<\/b>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Known to relieve <\/span><b>nausea, stress, and fatigue<\/b>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h3><b>Processing &amp; Quality<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At <\/span><b>Bombay Foodstuff<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, we procure mace directly from trusted farms in <\/span><b>Kerala and Southern India<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, ensuring high purity, freshness, and natural aroma. Our mace is carefully dried, sorted, and packaged to meet <\/span><b>international export standards<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for the food, spice, and flavoring industries.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>Producing States<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Kerala, Tamil Nadu, and parts of Karnataka<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>Packaging Options<\/b><\/h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Whole Mace Blades \u2013 bulk or retail packs<\/span>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ground Mace Powder \u2013 customized mesh size for food manufacturers<\/span>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Private labeling available for global B2B clients<\/span>&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><b>Bombay Foodstuff delivers premium-quality Mace (Javitri) with authentic flavor, hygienic processing, and export-ready packaging \u2013 trusted by chefs, spice traders, and food industries worldwide.<\/b><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mace, the dried aril of nutmeg, offers a warm, aromatic, and slightly sweet flavor. Widely used in baked goods, soups, sauces, curries, and spice blends, it adds refined depth to cuisines worldwide. Rich in essential oils and nutrients, our mace is hygienically processed, export-quality, and available in whole blades or ground powder.<\/span><\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":1027,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false},"product_brand":[],"product_cat":[25],"product_tag":[],"class_list":["post-814","product","type-product","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","product_cat-uncategorized","first","instock","shipping-taxable","product-type-simple"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/bombayfoodstuff.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/product\/814","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/bombayfoodstuff.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/product